{"id": "EUVD-2026-103472", "enisaUuid": "2c7ad74a-c441-374a-b969-8dd632caf736", "description": "cgltf through 1.15 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in cgltf_accessor_unpack_floats() that advances the sparse values cursor by the base bufferView byteStride. Attackers can supply a crafted glTF or GLB file that passes cgltf_validate() to read adjacent heap memory into vertex data or crash applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T17:42:50", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/cgltf-accessor-unpack-floats-sparse-oob", "https://github.com/jkuhlmann/cgltf/blob/360db1a95480fe102ae9c69b27c5d101167ff5ba/cgltf.h#L2436-L2441", "https://github.com/jkuhlmann/cgltf/blob/360db1a95480fe102ae9c69b27c5d101167ff5ba/cgltf.h#L1612-L1619", "https://github.com/jkuhlmann/cgltf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cgltf-through-1.15-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-cgltf-accessor-unpack-floats"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wfq9-23x4-jh5f", "CVE-2026-112019"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14679d7d-be0d-35a9-864a-2d91c6fa37bb", "product": {"name": "cgltf", "vendor": {"name": "jkuhlmann"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fa8ff8e6-8c4c-3621-8f08-6f1bc2e69c8d", "vendor": {"name": "jkuhlmann"}}], "isExploited": false}